def h(i,s,w,o,v,b=True):
 d['assumptions'].append(dict(id=i,statement=s,why=w,owner=o,validation=v,launchBlocker=b))
h('H1','Release one recommends eligible amounts and routes all decisions to authorized insurer adjudicators; it cannot issue payment, deny coverage or notify claimants.','Unknown authority and policy interpretation require a bounded useful release.','Claims product owner','Approve assist-only scope and identify adjudicator roles.')
h('H2','A tenant policy registry provides legally reviewed immutable policy/endorsement versions, effective intervals, member binding and explicit claim-date selection rules.','Upload text alone cannot establish governing coverage.','Insurance policy lead','Approve temporal rule packs, member coverage lookup and retrospective amendment handling.')
h('H3','Synthetic rule pack HC1 uses admission-date selection, inclusive discharge day, INR minor units, room-rent cap only on room lines, no proportional deduction, zero deductible and zero coinsurance.','A concrete executable illustration is needed; none of these are verified insurer rules.','Insurance policy lead','Replace or approve every rule; validate day count, benefit sublimits, exclusions, coordination, remaining sum insured, rounding and temporal basis per product.')
h('H4','Internal case store supports tenant scoped transactions, optimistic versions, immutable evidence hashes, durable outbox and operation lookup. All external adapters remain unverified.','Recovery and audit require durable state.','Platform owner','Contract spike proving version CAS, transactional events, idempotency and readback with access controls.')
h('H5','Use restricted medical evidence storage, encrypted transport and storage, tenant keys, no provider training, no raw content in logs; proposed 30-day working-copy deletion after case close subject to insurer approved retention/legal holds.','Medical data needs explicit minimization and a verified retention basis.','Privacy owner','Approve lawful basis, residency, model processing contract, access matrix, retention and legal-hold policy before real data.')
h('H6','Human queues are staffed by claims operations: acknowledge in 4 elapsed hours, review in 2 elapsed days; overdue goes to duty manager at 4h and head of claims at 48h. Timers run UTC 24x7.','Missing information and exceptions need an owned end state.','Claims operations lead','Confirm staffing, escalation channels, queue capacity and elapsed-time SLA.')
h('H7','Illustrative volume is 1000 cases/month; 80% reach the model and 5% of reached cases need one schema repair retry. Synthetic standard model prices are USD 2 input and USD 8 output per million tokens.','Provides reproducible capacity/cost hypotheses, not measured provider prices.','Engineering lead','Measure branch mix, token distribution, throughput and approved model quote.',False)
h('H8','Proposed release quality gates are zero safety failures in fixed synthetic guard suite, 99% line arithmetic agreement, 98% supported evidence precision and 20% median handling-time reduction.','Explicit hypotheses support go/no-go decisions; do not claim proven benefits.','Claims product owner','Baseline measurement, representative held-out evaluation and sign-off on targets.',False)
h('H9','Scope is one insurer product, one currency per claim and machine-readable or supported scanned inpatient reimbursement claims. Appeals, fraud decisions, outpatient, multi-currency and medical necessity decisions are human-only.','Limits initial policy complexity and avoids pretending to give medical advice.','Claims product owner','Approve product/language/OCR support manifest and exception routing.')
